<!--
  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Milos Vasic
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  iter-71 EMERGENCY: Proper adaptive-icon foreground vector.

  Canvas: 108dp × 108dp (required by the adaptive-icon spec).
  Safe zone: 72dp × 72dp centered, i.e. 18dp inset on all sides.
  The "Y" glyph is drawn to fit within the 72×72 safe zone
  (viewport coords 18–90) so it is never clipped by any launcher mask.

  Used by:
    mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml        (foreground + monochrome)
    mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher_round.xml  (foreground + monochrome)

  This file also serves the monochrome layer (Android 13+ renders the
  MONOCHROME layer as a single-color tinted shape; the foreground layer
  is rendered as-authored without tint).

  iter-91 forensic case: the iter-71 fix authored the path with
  android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF" on the assumption "tinted at runtime by
  the system". Only the MONOCHROME layer is tinted; the FOREGROUND layer
  rendered as solid white on the white ic_launcher_background → invisible
  icon on every Android launcher and on the system "All files access" /
  app-info screens. The installable_app_icon_challenge PASSed because it
  only checked vector structure (path present, no @mipmap/ reference) —
  not that the foreground color contrasts with the background. Operator-
  visible result: blank white circle where the Y should be.

  Fix: foreground fillColor = Yole brand red (#D32F2F) — high contrast
  against the white background, on-brand. The monochrome layer reuses
  the same vector but Android 13+ ignores the fillColor and tints with
  the system accent, so the brand color choice only affects the
  foreground layer.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!--
      "Y" letterform centered in the 72dp safe zone (viewport 18..90).
      Geometry:
        The glyph spans x: 24..84, y: 22..86 (comfortably inside safe zone).
        Two diagonal arms descend from top-left / top-right to a central stem,
        then the stem drops straight down to the baseline.

        Arm widths: 10 units
        Stem width: 10 units centered at x=54
        Top of arms: y=22
        Join point (center): x=54, y=56
        Baseline: y=86
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFD32F2F"
        android:pathData="
          M 24,22
          L 49,56
          L 49,86
          L 59,86
          L 59,56
          L 84,22
          L 73,22
          L 54,49
          L 35,22
          Z
        "/>

</vector>
